    },
    {
      "name": "hmacKeyedVerify",
      "reason": "the same check as hmacSha256Verify over an absorbed HmacKey and a window of a buffer, held by tests/link/crypto_jwt (\"HmacKey: hmacKeyedVerify accepts the tag it made\"); its message is a (data, off, len) /* window */, but its first parameter is the class HmacKey, which vector 0.6.0 refuses in a ts-interface block (\"HmacKey is not a ts-interface type; use u8[], string, boolean, i8, i16, i32, i64, u8, u16, u32, u64, f64, Secret<u8[]>, u16[], u32[], u64[], each optionally | null\"), and its tag is a (tag, tagAt) pair read in place, which neither a window nor an /* out CAP */ write declares"
    },
    {
      "name": "pbkdf2HmacSha256",
      "reason": "PBKDF2 (RFC 8018), which uses HMAC-SHA-256 as its PRF but is a different function, with its own vectors and none in RFC 4231"
    },
